   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Come_Clean_%28Puddle_of_Mudd_album%29",
   "resumo_en": "Come Clean is the second studio album and major label debut by the American rock band Puddle of Mudd. It was released on August 28, 2001, through Flawless Records. The album broke Puddle of Mudd into the mainstream, featuring the singles \"Control\", \"Blurry\", \"Drift & Die\" and \"She Hates Me\". Various tracks were re-recorded from the band's previous releases, Stuck and Abrasive.\nCome Clean was the band's biggest hit on the US Billboard 200, peaking at number nine. The album has sold over 5,000,000 copies and was certified 3× Platinum by the RIAA."
